.TH XCHROOT 1 "2026-09-07" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xchroot \- enter a prepared chroot environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xchroot
.I chroot-dir
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xchroot
mounts the filesystems needed by a chroot and executes a command inside it. It mounts or binds \fB/dev\fR, \fB/proc\fR, \fB/sys\fR, \fB/run\fR, \fB/tmp\fR, and \fB@SYSCONFDIR@/resolv.conf\fR as appropriate, then cleans up mounts on exit.
.PP
If COMMAND is omitted, \fB/usr/bin/sh\fR is launched. Arguments are passed without collapsing their structure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
xchroot /mnt/mysystem
xchroot /mnt/mysystem portsync
xchroot /mnt/mysystem @PROJECT_NAME@ sysup -y
xchroot /mnt/mysystem /usr/bin/mksh -c portsync
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on successful command execution; non-zero for invalid directories, mount failures, permission errors, or command failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chroot (1),
.BR @PROJECT_NAME@ (1)
